1. Intercloud & Cloud Federation
	Definition: An interconnected "cloud of clouds" enabling resource sharing, workload migration, and data exchange across distinct Cloud Service Providers3031.
	Classifications:
	Federation of Clouds: Provider-managed interconnections where clouds rent excess capacity from one another transparently to the user3233.
	Multicloud: Client-managed deployments where the consumer explicitly integrates services across multiple distinct providers33.
	Topologies: Centralized Intercloud Federation vs. Peer-to-Peer Intercloud Federation33.
	Benefits: Prevents vendor lock-in, expands geographic reach, enhances application fault-tolerance, and optimizes energy consumption via cross-data-center VM migration31more_horiz.
	Challenges: Establishing trust mechanisms, unifying billing models, cross-provider SLA enforcement, and identity federation3135. Uses open standards like XMPP, OCCI, and CIMI3536.
