2. Cloud Management & DMTF Reference Architecture
	Core Management Functions: Resource provisioning, Service Level Management (SLA tracking), cost optimization (auto-scaling, spot instances), and task orchestration3137.
	DMTF Reference Architecture Components:
	Cloud Service Developer: Designs and maintains service templates38.
	Cloud Service Consumer: Accesses and utilizes cloud services38.
	Cloud Service Provider: Supplies infrastructure and platform services38.
	Provider Interface & Profiles: Standardized specifications defining management domain properties38.
	Management Security: Centralized Cloud Management Platforms (CMPs) like AWS Console, OpenStack, and VMware vRealize represent high-value targets; compromising the management portal risks the entire enterprise infrastructure31more_horiz.
