3. Mobile Cloud Computing (MCC)
	Definition: An infrastructure where data storage and processing occur outside the mobile device, offloading heavy computations to cloud data centers or local cloudlets39more_horiz.
	Benefits: Extends smartphone battery life, overcomes local RAM/storage constraints, and improves app scalability and data reliability4142.
	Technical Challenges: High job offloading costs (bandwidth consumption), user mobility tracking across cellular networks, network latency, and live VM migration overheads41more_horiz.
